# MDC Rule: WordPress/PHP Performance Optimization

- Use object caching and transients to minimize repeated database queries.
- Minimize the use of expensive operations inside loops.
- Load scripts and styles conditionally only when needed.
- Avoid loading unnecessary plugins or themes.
- Use autoloading and Composer for dependency management where possible.
- Optimize database queries and use indexes appropriately.
- Profile and monitor performance using tools like Query Monitor.
- Use build tools to bundle and minify front-end assets; enqueue only optimized assets.

This rule applies to all *.php files in all subdirectories.

// Example: Enqueue minified asset
wp_enqueue_script(
    'my-plugin-main',
    plugins_url( 'assets/js/main.min.js', __FILE__ ),
    array( 'jquery' ),
    '1.0.0',
    true
);





